
     extern  unsigned int   All_mask;

     This is an integer bitmask that has a bit set for every
active user in the program.

     For example, if ports 1 and 3 are active, then All_mask
would contain 0A hex, or 10 decimal.  The binary representation
is:

     3          2         1
     10987654321098765432109876543210
     --------------------------------
     00000000000000000000000000010010

     (This assumes a 32 bit integer.  A machine with 16 bit integers,
like the IBM PC, would have a maximum of 16 users in the bit mask.)
